      "question": "My manager wants a quick look at the oil condition on Transformer 1 at site MAIN. From the latest reading and the stats over the full available window, give me dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oxygen, nitrogen and dbds, and say whether any of them moved in a direction that points to moisture ingress, air ingress or oil ageing. Rank the three concerns from most to least supported by the data. Don't use the combustible gases for this. If dielectric_rigidity or interfacial_v has no data, say so and base the ranking on oxygen and nitrogen only.",
      "answer": "**Oil condition snapshot \u2014 Transformer 1 (MAIN), window 2024-01-15 \u2192 2024-01-19 (5 readings)**\n\n| Sensor | Latest (01-19) | Full-window stats | Movement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| dielectric_rigidity (kV) | 55 | min 53, max 56, mean 54.6 | Oscillating \u00b11\u20132 kV, no trend |\n| interfacial_v (mN/m) | 45 | min 44, max 46, mean 45.0 | Flat, \u00b11 mN/m noise |\n| oxygen (ppm) | 5,850 | min 5,700, max 5,900, mean 5,822 | Up slightly from 5,860 on day 1 \u2014 no sustained rise |\n| nitrogen (ppm) | 27,850 | min 27,700, max 28,000, mean 27,868 | Up ~8 ppm from start; essentially flat |\n| dbds | 19 | min 18, max 20, mean 19.0 | Flat |\n\n**Interpretation (combustible gases excluded):**\n\n- **Moisture ingress** \u2014 No support. Dielectric rigidity (53\u201356 kV) and interfacial tension (44\u201346 mN/m) are both well within healthy ranges and show no downward trend; neither points to rising water in the oil.\n- **Air ingress** \u2014 Minimal support. Oxygen and nitrogen are both essentially flat day-to-day (variation < ~2%), with no coordinated upward drift you'd expect from ongoing air leakage into the conservator/oil.\n- **Oil ageing** \u2014 Least supported. Interfacial tension would typically fall and DBDS (oxidation byproducts) rise with ageing; both are stable with no upward DBDS trend.\n\n**Ranking (most \u2192 least supported):** 1) Air ingress (marginal \u2014 the only signals moving at all, oxygen and nitrogen, are trending very slightly up, but within noise), 2) Moisture ingress, 3) Oil ageing.\n\nOverall the oil looks stable \u2014 none of the three concerns is meaningfully supported by this window.",
