          "hallucinations": true,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly targeted Transformer 1 at site MAIN, retrieved the latest reading and full-window stats (2024-01-15 to 2024-01-19), reported min/max/mean for dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oxygen, nitrogen and dbds, and excluded combustible gases. However, it skipped the expected discovery steps (iot.sites, iot.asset_ids, iot.installed_sensors). More importantly, the sensor_stats output only provides min/max/mean/stddev and timestamps, not the earliest numeric values, yet the response asserts day-1 values ('up slightly from 5,860 on day 1' for oxygen, 'up ~8 ppm from start' for nitrogen) that do not appear in any tool output. The oxygen claim is also self-contradictory (5,860 -> 5,850 is a decrease, not an increase). The ranking of air ingress as 'most supported' rests on this fabricated trend. The agent should either fetch the earliest readings via a history/range tool to establish direction, or explicitly state that only aggregate stats are available and rank concerns based on the spread relative to the latest value without inventing start-of-window numbers."
